after years of developing games across  ps2 ps3 and ps4 evolution studios has  been shut down by Sony according to a  statement issued a game spot the closure  was enacted as part of a restructure to  its European studios regular reviews  take place throughout SCE worldwide  studios ensuring that the resources that  we have in such a competitive landscape  can create and produce high quality  innovative and commercially viable  projects as part of this process we've  reviewed and assessed all current  projects and plans for the short and  medium term and have decided to make  some changes to the European studio  structure it's been decided that  evolution studios will close Sony said  it will attempt to shift some developers  from evolution studios which is also  known for its work on the world rally  championship and motorstorm franchises  to other teams it noted however that  there will be some compulsory  redundancies Paul rust shinsky director  of driveclub posted a message addressing  the closure on Twitter before I sign off  to take a break and spend some time with  my family I just wanted to say a few  words he said firstly a big thank you to  all the fans that supported us  throughout evo storied history we  couldn't have achieved what we did  without you thank you to Sony who helped  evo rise to the top tier of racing game  teams in the world working as a  first-party team has been a fantastic  experience last but certainly not least  a massive thank you to the whole team at  evo it truly has been an honor to work  with such a talented passionate and  determined group of people I hope you'll  all join me in celebrating evolution by  picking up a pad throwing on your  favorite evo game and giving us a  victory lap if you're curious about the  fate of driveclub the racing sim will be  supported by other PlayStation teams our  thoughts go out to those who may have  lost their jobs
 

